 "result": "All 3 tests pass.\n\n**Fix**: `Sentinel` (in `src/click/_utils.py`) is an `enum.Enum` whose members hold plain `object()` values. `Enum.__reduce_ex__` pickles by reconstructing `cls(self._value_)`, but a freshly unpickled `object()` isn't the same instance as the original, so `Sentinel(new_object)` raised `ValueError: ... is not a valid Sentinel`. `copy`/`deepcopy` already worked since `Enum.__copy__`/`__deepcopy__` just return `self`.\n\nAdded `Sentinel.__reduce_ex__` to reconstruct via `getattr(cls, name)` instead of by value, so pickling round-trips to the same singleton member. Added a regression test covering `copy`, `deepcopy`, and `pickle` at every protocol for both `UNSET` and `FLAG_NEEDS_VALUE`.",
